# PART 1 — WHAT IS THINKNET?

## 1.1 Vision

ThinkNet is an AI research and engineering organization focused on understanding, developing, improving and advancing artificial intelligence, particularly Large Language Models (LLMs).

Our ambition is not simply to build another chatbot or model-training interface.

We want to develop an extensive AI research ecosystem containing:

- AI research infrastructure.
- Model training infrastructure.
- Agentic training systems.
- Interactive learning environments.
- Synthetic data generation systems.
- Knowledge distillation infrastructure.
- Kernel and computational optimization tools.
- Model architecture experimentation tools.
- Multimodal intelligence environments.
- Evaluation and benchmarking systems.
- Model interpretability and inspection systems.
- Autonomous AI research agents.
- Generative AI infrastructure.
- Low-level model engineering tools.

The central idea is to create an environment in which AI models can learn, experiment, interact, develop capabilities, receive feedback and continuously improve.

ThinkNet will investigate how we can develop more capable, efficient, reliable and intelligent models through better training methodologies, architectures, data, environments and computational engineering.

## 1.2 Core Philosophy

Our philosophy:

**Don't just train models on information. Give them environments in which they can develop capabilities.**

Traditional training frequently relies on static datasets.

ThinkNet wants to investigate a broader approach involving:

1. High-quality pretraining data.
2. Synthetic data generation.
3. Interactive environments.
4. Structured episodes.
5. Realistic task execution.
6. AI-agent-assisted training.
7. Automated evaluation.
8. Feedback-driven learning.
9. Distillation and post-training.
10. Computational optimization.

We want models to develop capabilities through both information and experience.

