# PART 3 — AGENTIC RESEARCH & TRAINING SYSTEM

## 3.1 Core Concept

AI agents will actively participate throughout the model development and training lifecycle.

They will not simply execute isolated tasks.

They will observe, inspect, analyze, investigate, generate experiments, evaluate results and recommend improvements.

The long-term objective is to develop an AI-assisted research and training infrastructure in which specialized agents work together.

## 3.2 Specialized Agents

### A. Training Supervisor Agent

Responsibilities:

- Monitor training progress.
- Coordinate specialized agents.
- Track experiments.
- Identify unusual behaviour.
- Organize training iterations.
- Recommend improvements.

### B. Training Inspector Agent

Responsibilities:

- Inspect training loss.
- Monitor validation loss.
- Analyze gradient statistics.
- Monitor GPU utilization.
- Inspect memory consumption.
- Detect training instability.
- Generate diagnostic reports.

### C. Data Research Agent

Responsibilities:

- Generate synthetic data.
- Analyze dataset quality.
- Detect duplicates.
- Identify weak data categories.
- Recommend data mixtures.
- Generate targeted examples.
- Organize training curricula.

### D. Kernel Optimization Agent

Responsibilities:

- Analyze computational bottlenecks.
- Inspect kernel performance.
- Recommend optimization opportunities.
- Compare kernel implementations.
- Benchmark memory usage.
- Report execution efficiency.

### E. Model Research Agent

Responsibilities:

- Inspect model architecture.
- Analyze layer behaviour.
- Study attention patterns.
- Investigate model weaknesses.
- Propose architecture experiments.
- Analyze internal representations.

### F. Evaluation Agent

Responsibilities:

- Run reasoning benchmarks.
- Test coding capabilities.
- Evaluate mathematics.
- Analyze tool-use performance.
- Detect capability regressions.
- Compare checkpoints.
- Identify improvement opportunities.

### G. Post-Training Agent

Responsibilities:

- Prepare SFT experiments.
- Investigate distillation.
- Analyze reward signals.
- Prepare preference datasets.
- Evaluate post-training results.
- Compare model capabilities.

## 3.3 Three Levels of Agent Autonomy

**Level 1 — Observer**

Agents can inspect, measure, monitor and report.

**Level 2 — Researcher**

Agents can investigate problems, develop hypotheses and propose experiments.

**Level 3 — Operator**

Agents can execute approved experiments, modify configurations and manage bounded workflows.

Initially, consequential changes require human approval.

Autonomous operations must have validation, resource limits, experiment logs and rollback mechanisms.

## 3.4 Continuous Training Intelligence Loop

The system should operate throughout training.

Before training:
- Inspect configurations.
- Analyze datasets.
- Check architecture.
- Estimate computational requirements.

During training:
- Monitor metrics.
- Inspect computational performance.
- Analyze training stability.
- Track resource consumption.

At checkpoints:
- Evaluate capabilities.
- Inspect internal model behaviour.
- Compare results.

Between experiments:
- Identify weaknesses.
- Generate hypotheses.
- Recommend improvements.
- Prepare new experiments.

Next iteration:
- Execute approved improvements.
- Compare outcomes.
- Record findings.

The objective is a continuous, measurable research cycle.

