# PART 4 — THE THINKNET ENVIRONMENT ECOSYSTEM

This is one of ThinkNet's most important research directions.

We want to create a large ecosystem of interactive environments in which LLMs can develop specialized capabilities.

These environments should not be limited to text-based exercises.

They should include real software, simulations, professional tools, scientific workflows, engineering systems, visual environments and complex tasks.

## 4.1 Standard Environment Hierarchy

Every environment follows this hierarchy:

ENVIRONMENT → EPISODES → TASKS → EVALUATION → FEEDBACK

**Environment:** A complete learning domain.

**Episode:** A focused learning experience designed to develop a particular capability.

**Task:** An individual assignment within an episode.

**Evaluation:** Measures the quality of execution.

**Feedback:** Identifies mistakes and provides information for improvement.

An episode can contain hundreds or thousands of different tasks.

