# PART 15 — ENGINEERING PRINCIPLES

All development should follow these principles.

### 1. Modular Architecture

Every component should have a defined responsibility and reusable interfaces.

### 2. Interoperability

Different environments should be able to communicate through standard interfaces.

### 3. Reproducibility

Experiments must be traceable and repeatable.

### 4. Measurable Improvement

Never claim that an optimization works without benchmarking it.

### 5. Model-Agnostic Design

Where practical, support different model architectures and providers.

### 6. Resource Awareness

Training and experiments must consider available compute, memory and cost.

### 7. Safety

Use sandboxed execution for code, controlled access for computer-use agents, synthetic data for sensitive enterprise tasks and human approval for consequential actions.

### 8. Evidence-Based Research

Distinguish established techniques, hypotheses, experimental findings and unverified claims.

### 9. Reusable Infrastructure

Build systems that support many environments rather than one-off implementations.

### 10. Scientific Documentation

Record decisions, failures, results and lessons.

